+# daily-summary Specification
+
+## Purpose
+TBD - created by archiving change daily-summary-and-login-rate-limiting. Update Purpose after archive.
+## Requirements
+### Requirement: Daily summary endpoint
+
+The system SHALL expose `GET /api/summary/today` (requires authentication). It SHALL NOT accept a
+`?user=<username>` parameter and SHALL always compute the summary for the authenticated caller
+only (`ClaimsFromCtx`), the same self-only scoping as `nutrition-target`'s endpoint, since its
+inputs include the caller's own settings and food log.
+
+"Today" SHALL be the caller's current Local Day as defined by `food-day-completeness`'s "Local Day
+boundary" requirement (the caller's stored `timezone` setting, UTC fallback for a missing or
+invalid value) — this endpoint SHALL NOT define "today" any other way.
+
+On success the system SHALL return HTTP 200 with:
+- `date`: the resolved Local Day, `YYYY-MM-DD`.
+- `calories_consumed`, `protein_grams_consumed`, `carbs_grams_consumed`, `fat_grams_consumed`: the
+  sum of those fields across the caller's `FoodMeal` rows whose Logged Day is today and whose
+  `status` is `confirmed`. Rows in any other status SHALL be excluded from these sums (their macro
+  fields are not populated until confirmation).
+- `meal_count`: a count of the caller's `FoodMeal` rows whose Logged Day is today, regardless of
+  `status`.
+- `last_updated`: the maximum `logged_at` among the caller's `FoodMeal` rows whose Logged Day is
+  today, regardless of `status`, or `null` if there are none.
+- `display_language`: the caller's current `display_language` setting, using its existing
+  resolution/default rules (see `display-language`).
+- `target`: an embedded object, either `{"available": true, "calories", "protein_grams",
+  "carbs_grams", "fat_grams"}` computed identically to `nutrition-target`'s "Nutrition Target
+  computation" requirement, or `{"available": false, "reason": "<reason>"}` using the same four
+  reason codes and precondition ordering as `nutrition-target`'s endpoint requirement
+  (`missing_profile`, `missing_measurements`, `missing_goal_weight`,
+  `insufficient_activity_data`). This endpoint SHALL NOT return HTTP 422 for an unavailable
+  target — an unavailable target is a normal, expected state on this endpoint, and the response
+  SHALL still be HTTP 200 with `target.available = false`, so the caller can render
+  `calories_consumed` regardless of whether a target exists.
+- `recommendation`: always `null` in this change. No requirement in this change computes a
+  non-null value for this field.
+
+#### Scenario: Full summary with an available target
+
+- **WHEN** an authenticated user with two confirmed meals logged today (combined 1,450 kcal) and a
+  fully computable nutrition target requests their summary
+- **THEN** the system SHALL return HTTP 200 with `calories_consumed = 1450`, `meal_count = 2`,
+  `target.available = true`, and the four target fields populated
+
+#### Scenario: Consumed totals exclude unconfirmed meals
+
+- **GIVEN** a user has one `confirmed` meal (500 kcal) and one `pending_review` meal logged today
+- **WHEN** the system computes `calories_consumed`
+- **THEN** the result is 500, not the sum including the unconfirmed meal, and `meal_count` is 2
+
+#### Scenario: No meals logged today
+
+- **WHEN** an authenticated user with no `FoodMeal` rows on today's Local Day requests their
+  summary
+- **THEN** the system SHALL return HTTP 200 with `calories_consumed = 0`,
+  `protein_grams_consumed = 0`, `carbs_grams_consumed = 0`, `fat_grams_consumed = 0`,
+  `meal_count = 0`, and `last_updated = null`
+
+#### Scenario: Target unavailable does not fail the request
+
+- **GIVEN** a user has never saved a `birthdate` or `sex`
+- **WHEN** they request their summary
+- **THEN** the system SHALL return HTTP 200 (not 422) with `target = {"available": false, "reason":
+  "missing_profile"}`, and `calories_consumed`/`meal_count`/`last_updated` SHALL still reflect
+  today's actual meals
+
+#### Scenario: Recommendation is always null
+
+- **WHEN** any authenticated user requests their summary
+- **THEN** the response's `recommendation` field SHALL be `null`
+
+#### Scenario: Unauthenticated request rejected
+
+- **WHEN** a request to `GET /api/summary/today` carries no valid token
+- **THEN** the system SHALL return HTTP 401
+
+#### Scenario: A processing meal still updates last_updated and meal_count
+
+- **GIVEN** a user has a single meal logged today whose status is `processing` (photo uploaded,
+  recognition not yet complete)
+- **WHEN** they request their summary
+- **THEN** `meal_count = 1` and `last_updated` equals that meal's `logged_at`, even though
+  `calories_consumed = 0` because the meal is not yet `confirmed`
+
